# Shell scripts keep LF endings on every platform: a CRLF shebang line, which a
# Windows checkout would otherwise introduce when core.autocrlf is on, makes the
# interpreter fail to start.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Formats this repository commits as binary, declared rather than inferred.
#
# Git guesses binary from content, and what it guesses on is a NUL byte, so
# without these lines "is this file binary?" and "does this file contain a NUL?"
# are the same question and a gate cannot use one to judge the other.
# ci/gates/no-nul-bytes.py reads these declarations for that reason.
#
# Declaring them also stops git trying to diff or merge them as text. A new
# binary format needs a line here; a file that needs a NUL and is NOT one of
# these formats almost certainly wants an escape instead.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.jar  binary
*.gz   binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
